# PandaCSS — Patterns

Patterns are layout primitives that compile to flat CSS — no runtime cost. Built-ins: `stack`, `vstack`, `hstack`, `flex`, `grid`, `gridItem`, `box`, `container`, `wrap`, `aspectRatio`, `divider`, `spacer`, `square`, `circle`, `center`, `linkOverlay`, `float`, `bleed`, `visuallyHidden`, `cq`.

## Usage at call site

```tsx
import { stack, container } from "styled-system/patterns"

<div className={stack({ gap: "4", align: "stretch" })}>
  <Header />
  <Body />
</div>

<section className={container({ maxW: "5xl", py: "12" })}>
  ...
</section>
```

Or as JSX (with `jsxFramework` enabled):

```tsx
<Stack gap="4">...</Stack>
```

## Custom pattern

```ts
// src/theme/preset/patterns/container-grid.ts
import { definePattern } from "@pandacss/dev"

export const containerGrid = definePattern({
  description: "Centered container with responsive padding",
  properties: {
    columns: { type: "number" },
    gap: { type: "token", value: "spacing" },
  },
  transform(props) {
    return {
      display: "grid",
      maxWidth: "88rem",
      mx: "auto",
      px: { base: "4", md: "8" },
      gridTemplateColumns: `repeat(${props.columns ?? 12}, 1fr)`,
      gap: props.gap,
    }
  },
})
```

Register in `panda.config.ts` via `theme.extend.patterns` or a preset.

## Rules

- Prefer patterns over hand-rolled flex/grid `css()` calls — patterns are intent-named and reusable.
- Custom patterns belong in `theme/preset/patterns/` and wire through `presets`, not inline in `panda.config.ts`.
- `properties` types: `boolean`, `number`, `string`, `enum`, `token` (with `value` pointing at a token category).
- `transform` returns a Panda style object — full token + condition support.

